	"description": "An extensively rebuilt version of the classic WebGL fluid simulation, tuned for OLED and wide-gamut displays.\r\n\r\n[h1]Features[/h1]\r\n[list]\r\n[*] Display-P3 wide gamut rendering + optional HDR-mode compensation (auto-detects Windows HDR)\r\n[*] Soft-knee brightness compression and saturation restore: colors stay pure, never wash to white or mud\r\n[*] Autonomous wanderer splats with screen-fullness governor: paints, pauses, decays, repaints on its own\r\n[*] Survivor wanderer + separating dart keep compositions evolving while the field rests\r\n[*] Duty-cycled hue-shift bursts rotate the whole palette on a schedule\r\n[*] Hold left mouse to pour dye; every behavior above is a slider\r\n[/list]\r\n\r\n[h1]Notes[/h1]\r\nDye Resolution ships at 4096 for maximum detail - lower it to 1024/512 on weaker GPUs.\r\nAuthor's Wallpaper Engine color settings (right panel, optional): saturation 57, contrast 67, brightness 53, hue 54.\r\nLooks best on an OLED in a dim room with Windows HDR on.\r\n\r\n[h1]Credits[/h1]\r\nBased on PavelDoGreat's WebGL-Fluid-Simulation (MIT): https://github.com/PavelDoGreat/WebGL-Fluid-Simulation\r\nWallpaper Engine port by Delivator: https://github.com/Delivator/WebGL-Fluid-Simulation\r\nFPS limiter by fuchst. Extended feature set built on top of both.",
